ons says there are more than  1.4 million registered afghans living in  pakistan and an estimated 2 million more  are undocumented  and though the thalibond insists it's  more moderate than it used to be the  group has said it will not tolerate  music in public and artists like shams  raheel crossed into pakistan leaving  behind their loved ones fearing for  their lives  this room is where shams raheel lives  and works on the walls there are posters  showing what his life was like before  the taliban took over afghanistan  he was a famous musician who lived in  kabul and had tv performances  but after the coup he feared for his  life and fled to live with relatives in  pakistan  he had to leave his family behind  now he only sees his son during video  calls  [Music]  my son called me from afghanistan and  asked when i'll be home he's only three  years old and he wants to know where his  dad is  i always tell him i'm in a nearby city  and we'll be home soon  he doesn't know i'm in pakistan  my wife also has a lot of questions  she wants to know what she should do now  next door a fellow refugee allows him to  use his room to cook  the taliban has forbidden music in  afghanistan so life has become dangerous  for musicians who decide to  and then i escaped my home country  shams gives his cousin hamza music  lessons  the young man left afghanistan first  shams was able to follow him and now his  cousin hamza covers all his costs  when i called him up in afghanistan it  sounded like he was at his wit's end  i borrowed some money and sent it to him  so that he could come to pakistan  without the help of his relatives charms  wouldn't have been able to be in  pakistan  they've been here for four years already  and have established themselves once in  a while they invite him to dinner  but charm sees no future for himself in  pakistan he has no income and his family  is far away  at least i can get some sleep here  in afghanistan i used to lay awake at  night afraid of wha